\title{An order that shows nothing and strikes only when enough size appears at an acceptable price}
\description{
It is the closest thing to a minimum-quantity order that anyone can build: it waits until the visible book covers \code{minimum_quantity} at \code{limit_price} or better, and then sends an order for it. It answers HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed} and sends nothing to a broker until it fires, so keep the \code{parent_id} from the answer. The strike is rounded down to whole lots and uses the template's validity, so with the default \code{day} an unfilled strike rests at \code{limit_price}. A book UBI marks stale is never acted on.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
